TASK-260720-12iigs,task,compiled-artifact-schemas,Add build receipt v1 and install marker v2 schemas,backlog,STORY-260720-35dck7,,"Define the portable compiled-artifact metadata contracts. The receipt binds the exact logical build input, target, toolchain, fixed policy, and derived artifact identity. Marker v2 records build roots, raw build-source identity, sorted build records, cache keys, receipt hashes, and artifact paths while remaining readable alongside marker v1.","Work in curator-spec origin/main commit 57c1f56846d221ecc55786bd3c2467ec32f11730. Own new schemas/v1/build-receipt-v1.schema.json and schemas/v1/install-marker-v2.schema.json plus only the supporting definitions required in schemas/v1/common.schema.json after TASK-260720-wajgn8. Keep install-marker-v1.schema.json untouched. Physical manager-home paths, cache filenames, locks, and storage backends are not schema fields.","build-receipt-v1 is strict and requires schema version, cache key, the complete canonical go-v1 input including curator-build-source-v1, build_root, command, source_dir, native target and tuning, curator-go-toolchain-v1, fixed policy, and one manager-derived artifact path, hash, and size; receipt fields cannot assert trusted provenance and unknown fields fail; install-marker-v2 supports skill_schema_version through 6, requires sorted build_roots and builds, requires build_source exactly when builds are non-empty, and records driver, cache key, receipt hash, artifact hash, and derived relative path per command; marker v1 remains valid and unchanged for legacy installs; new schema references resolve and python3 tools/validate.py passes.",[],[],[],,2026-07-20T01:44:31Z,2026-07-20T01:44:31Z,false,[],[],[]
